var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat","page":"Home","text":"The RegularlySampledFormat package provides an interface for working with RSF files.\n\nThe RSF file format is used in the Madagascar open-source package for geophysical data analysis.\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.Input-Tuple{String}","page":"Home","text":"Input(tag::String) -> Input\n\nCreate an instance of the Input struct for reading from an RSF file specified by tag.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.Input"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.Output-Tuple{String}","page":"Home","text":"Output(tag::String) -> Output\n\nCreate an instance of the Output struct for writing to an RSF file specified by tag.    \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.Output"},{"category":"type","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat._RSF","page":"Home","text":"_RSF(inp::Bool, tag=nothing) -> _RSF\n\nCreate an instance of the `_RSF` struct for reading or writing RSF files. \nIf `inp` is true, the function reads from an input RSF file specified by `tag`. \nIf `inp` is false, it prepares for writing to an output RSF file specified by `tag`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat._RSF"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.Datapath-Tuple{}","page":"Home","text":"Datapath() -> String\n\nReturn the path to the data directory. The path is determined by checking the following sources in order of priority:\n1. The environment variable `DATAPATH`.\n2. A file named `.datapath` in the current working directory.\n3. A file named `.datapath` in the user's home directory.\n4. If none of the above sources provide a path, the function defaults to returning\nthe current working directory (`\"./\"`).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.Datapath"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.Temp-Tuple{}","page":"Home","text":"Temp() -> (String, IO)\n\nCreate a temporary data path. The temporary data path is determined by checking the following sources in order of priority:\n1. The environment variable `TMPDATAPATH`.\n2. The result of `Datapath()` function.\n\nReturns a tuple containing the path to the temporary file and an IO object for writing to the file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.Temp"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.add!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat.SimTab, String}","page":"Home","text":"add!(t, keyval)\n\nEnter a key-value pair into the symbolic table `t` from a string of the form \"key=val\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.add!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.bytes-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF}","page":"Home","text":"bytes(rsf::_RSF) -> Int\n\nReturn the size in bytes of the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct. \nIf the data name is \"stdin\", it returns -1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.bytes"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.dataread!-Tuple{Input, Array}","page":"Home","text":"dataread!(inp::Input, data::Array)\n\nRead data from the RSF file represented by the `Input` struct into the provided `data` array.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.dataread!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.datawrite-Tuple{Output, Array}","page":"Home","text":"datawrite(out::Output, data::Array)\n\nWrite data from the provided `data` array to the RSF file represented by the `Output` struct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.datawrite"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.enter!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat.SimTab, String, String}","page":"Home","text":"enter!(t, key, val)\n\nEnter a key-value pair into the symbolic table `t`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.enter!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.fileflush!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, Union{Symbol, RegularlySampledFormat._RSF}}","page":"Home","text":"fileflush!(rsf::_RSF, src::_RSF)\n\nFlush the contents of the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct to disk. \nIf `src` is provided, it also flushes the contents of the source RSF file to the destination.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.fileflush!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.floatread!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, Any}","page":"Home","text":"floatwrite(rsf::_RSF, arr)\n\nWrite an array of floats (Float32) to the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.floatread!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.floatwrite-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, Any}","page":"Home","text":"floatwrite(rsf::_RSF, arr)\n\nWrite an array of floats (Float32) to the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.floatwrite"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.flush!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF}","page":"Home","text":"flush!(rsf::_RSF)\n\nFlush the contents of the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct to disk.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.flush!"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getbool","page":"Home","text":"getbool(key, default)\n\nExtract a boolean parameter from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getbool"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getbool-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat.SimTab, String}","page":"Home","text":"getbool(t, key)\n\nExtract a boolean parameter from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getbool"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getbools","page":"Home","text":"getbools(key, n, default)\n\nExtract an array of boolean parameters from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned. If the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getbools"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getbools-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat.SimTab, String, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"getbools(t, key, n)\n\nExtract an array of boolean parameters from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getbools"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getfilename-Tuple{IO}","page":"Home","text":"getfilename(stream::IO) -> Union{String, Symbol}\n\nFind the name of the file associated with the given IO stream. \nIf the stream is not associated with a file, returns `:none`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getfilename"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getfloat","page":"Home","text":"getfloat(key, default)\n\nExtract a float parameter from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getfloat"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getfloats","page":"Home","text":"getfloats(key, n, default)\n\nExtract an array of float parameters from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned. If the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getfloats"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getform-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF}","page":"Home","text":"getform(rsf::_RSF) -> String\n\nReturn the data format of the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getform"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getint","page":"Home","text":"getint(key, default)\n\nExtract an integer parameter from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getint"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getints","page":"Home","text":"getints(key, n, default)\n\nExtract an array of integer parameters from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned. If the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getints"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getpar","page":"Home","text":"getpar(p, key, T, default)\n\nExtract a parameter of type `T` from the parameter table `p` for a given `key`. \nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getpar"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getpar-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat.SimTab, String, DataType}","page":"Home","text":"getpar(t, key, T)\n\nExtract a parameter of type `T` from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getpar"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getpars","page":"Home","text":"getpars(p, key, n, T, default)\n\nExtract an array of parameters of type `T` from the parameter table `p` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned. If the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getpars"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getpars-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat.SimTab, String, Int64, DataType}","page":"Home","text":"getpars(t, key, n, T)\n\nExtract an array of parameters from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n` and will be of type `T`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getpars"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getprog-Tuple{Par}","page":"Home","text":"getprog(p)\n\nExtract the program name from the parameter table `p`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getprog"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getshape-Tuple{RSF}","page":"Home","text":"getshape(rsf)\n\nExtract the shape of the data array from the RSF file `rsf`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getshape"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getshape-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF}","page":"Home","text":"getshape(rsf::_RSF) -> Array{Int}\n\nExtract the shape of the data from the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct. \nThe function returns an array of integers representing the dimensions of the data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getshape"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getstring","page":"Home","text":"getstring(rsf::_RSF, key::String, default=:none) -> String\n\nRetrieve the string value associated with the specified `key` in the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct.\nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getstring"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getstring-2","page":"Home","text":"getstring(key, default)\n\nExtract a string parameter from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getstring"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getstring-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat.SimTab, String}","page":"Home","text":"getstring(t, key)\n\nExtract a string parameter from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getstring"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.gettype-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF}","page":"Home","text":"gettype(rsf::_RSF) -> DataType\n\nReturn the data type of the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.gettype"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.input!","page":"Home","text":"input!(t, filep)\n\nInput key-value pairs into the symbolic table `t` from a file stream `filep`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.input!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.intread!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, Any}","page":"Home","text":"intread!(rsf::_RSF, arr)  \n\nRead an array of integers (Int32) from the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct into the provided `arr`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.intread!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.intwrite-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, Any}","page":"Home","text":"intwrite(rsf::_RSF, arr)\n\nWrite an array of integers (Int32) to the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.intwrite"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.output-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat.SimTab, IOStream}","page":"Home","text":"output(t, filep)\n\nOutput the contents of the symbolic table `t` to a file stream `filep`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.output"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.putfloat!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, String, AbstractFloat}","page":"Home","text":"putfloat!(rsf::_RSF, key::String, val::Float32) -> Nothing\n\nWrite a float parameter to the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct. \nThe parameter is associated with the specified `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.putfloat!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.putfloats!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, String, Array{<:AbstractFloat}, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"putfloats!(rsf::_RSF,key::String,par::Array{Float32},n::Int)\n\nWrite an array of float parameters to the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct. \nThe parameters are associated with the specified `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.putfloats!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.putint!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, String, Integer}","page":"Home","text":"putint!(rsf::_RSF, key::String, par::Int)\n\nWrite an integer parameter to the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct. \nThe parameter is associated with the specified `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.putint!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.putints!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, String, Array{<:Integer}, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"putints!(rsf::_RSF, key::String, par::Array{Int}, n::Int)   \n\nWrite an array of integer parameters to the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct.\nThe parameters are associated with the specified `key`. The array has length `n`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.putints!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.putstring!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, String, String}","page":"Home","text":"putstring!(rsf::_RSF, key::String, par::String)\n\nWrite a string parameter to the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct. \nThe parameter is associated with the specified `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.putstring!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.setaformat!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, String, Int64, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"setaformat!(rsf::_RSF, format::String, line::Int=8, strip::Int=0)\n\nset a format for ASCII output\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.setaformat!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.setform!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, String}","page":"Home","text":"setform!(rsf::_RSF, form::String)\n\nSet the data format of the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct to `form`. \nIf `form` is \"ascii\", it also sets the appropriate formats for ASCII output.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.setform!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.setformat!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, String}","page":"Home","text":"setformat!(rsf::_RSF, dataformat::String)\n\nSet the data type and format of the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct based on the provided `dataformat` string. \nThe function determines the appropriate data type and format (ASCII, XDR, or native) based on the contents of `dataformat`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.setformat!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.settype!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, DataType}","page":"Home","text":"settype!(rsf::_RSF, T::DataType)\n\nSet the data type of the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct to `T`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.settype!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.string!-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat.SimTab, String}","page":"Home","text":"string!(t, string)\n\nEnter key-value pairs into the symbolic table `t` from a string of the form \"key1=val1 key2=val2 ...\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.string!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.tell-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF}","page":"Home","text":"tell(rsf::_RSF) -> Int\n\nReturn the current position in the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.tell"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.ucharwrite-Tuple{RegularlySampledFormat._RSF, Any}","page":"Home","text":"ucharwrite(rsf::_RSF, arr)\n\nWrite an array of unsigned chars (UInt8) to the RSF file represented by the `_RSF` struct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.ucharwrite"}]
}
